                <pb facs="0143" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.51A/59a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Diplomatic
                        Representatives in All Latin American Countries</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-25T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1919, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>At the instance of Secretary of Treasury inform Government to which you are
                    accredited that expenses of delegates sent to the Second Pan-American Financial
                    Conference to be held at Washington January 12 and 17, 1920, will be defrayed by
                    this Government during the period of their stay in Washington for the purposes
                    of the Conference. It is requested that delegates shall reach Washington not
                    later than the evening of January 9, 1920.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
